{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/963812-vampire-and-the-h-p-lovecraft-mythos","id":963812,"title":"Vampire and the H.P. Lovecraft Mythos","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-05T11:39:38-07:00","id":963812,"title":"Vampire and the H.P. Lovecraft Mythos","content":"I am doing some research as we speak to host a game to some friends and want to put in a Call of Cthulhu/Mythos feel to it. Chronicles of Darkness advertises that H.P. Lovecraft is a great way to run these games and want to go with it. However, most of the characters, are well...Vampires. Is it still possible to test the Integrity of a Vampire? Would they still be shocked by the H.P. Lovecraft Mythos? Since most Vampires have powers, how can you make them feel powerless to world that they already know?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10133-yarrumkin","name":"Yarrumkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10133_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T11:57:20-07:00","id":963824,"title":"","content":"I think the Chronicles of Darkness book suggests things more for mortal takes, but it's certainly possible to delve into cosmic horror with a vampire. They do have powers, but there's a limit to them, and there's no limit to the things a vampire can face in the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Just because you have powers doesn't mean they're going to be of any use, or worse, might become used against them. Ancient Bloodlines and Mysteries has the Edimmu, for instance. En-Isiratuu was a tyrant vampire king, and in order to fight against him the vampires of what would be the Circle of the Crone summoned spirits from beyond the stars and put them into a body, making what was essentially a star vampire. When it confronted En-Isiratuu, he found himself taken by an uncontrollable urge to drain the vampire, going so far as to commit diablerie, which he was known for doing at the time. Unfortunately, this was how the Edimmu 'Embraced,' and so he became the first subject of a vampiric scourge that spread across the land.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, going directly to Lovecraft, you have something like the Insects from Shaggai or the Mi-Go. Alien beings that 'possess' humanity, some for no other reason than their own hedonistic pleasure. Imagine the fun something like that could get up to with a vampire's body. It wouldn't even have to take full control, but what if after their daysleep the vampire wakes in strange places, with bodies living or dead, finding their body surrendered fully to some other being that didn't think enough about the Kindred to even try to communicate to it. Sure, you could tell another vampire, but that's likely to get you laughed out of your covenant, unless you're in the Ordo Dracul where it will get you put on a slab. You have some of this with the strix, though their reasons are more understandable.<br /> <br /> Basically, just because you're a vampire doesn't mean you can't be ignorant or taken by surprise, and just because of you have powers doesn't mean those powers will be universally useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T12:00:35-07:00","id":963826,"title":"","content":"Yes you can, don't forget that a starting vampire knows very little about what the over vampires do, they might start out thinking it's something the Circle pray to only to discover that a bunch of Dragons have been poking it to see what it does. As for them having powers so what? It outranks their powers or it responds to some Disiplines as if they were atempting to communicate or it can't be targeted by some Disiplines or it wants to give them more powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T16:19:36-07:00","id":963961,"title":"","content":"Have you read the Nosferatu entry in the 2e corebook? A few lines concerning &quot;the Gods Below&quot; sound like Lovecraft to me. And I certainly could see him writing about the Mission and what ever it is that they're into.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T20:59:31-07:00","id":964048,"title":"","content":"So would you say that making a Vampire game based on the Cthulhu mythos would be a good idea? This game is going to be centered on the premise of dealing with the cults of certain Cthulhu mythos Elder Gods. And most of my players if not all are used to playing the fantasy aspect of roleplaying games like Pathfinder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10133-yarrumkin","name":"Yarrumkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10133_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T21:15:55-07:00","id":964057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yarrumkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/963812-vampire-and-the-h-p-lovecraft-mythos?p=964048#post964048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So would you say that making a Vampire game based on the Cthulhu mythos would be a good idea?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say it's doable, whether or not it's a good idea is going to depend on the group. But go for it, the worst that happens is it doesn't work out so well and you change things up.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T01:22:39-07:00","id":964148,"title":"","content":"That sounds like an awesome basis. Honestly, the reason Vampire is my favourite line of WoD is because despite being immortal monsters, vampires are probably the most human of the creatures and the most normal. Their morality scale focuses on acting and feeling human (it used to be exactly the same as the human scale). They're not here for a reason, they don't have a designated enemy they can base their exstence around and they don't have a place to them, they don't belong anywhere. The closest thing they can call home is humanity and the default occupation for them, besides surviving, is to try to fit in. While powerful, they're also not THAT strong for most of them. Finally, they're numerous enough that they're nit really unique enough for that aspect to be a huge huge deal. Werewolves have a sacred duty to be super border patrol and, at least used to be supposed to run a territory, Changelings know Arcadia exists and that they have to be prepared for when the True Fae inevitably shows up. I don't know much about mages, but don't they have the thing with Atlantis ? They also have lots of realms they can go into and I think they're also pretty OP. Prometheans have a set goal (with differences of how to reach it) and they're generally too rare and messed up to form societies. Demons work against the God Mmachine. I don't know enough about the rest.<br /> <br /> I like vampires because they're the secret society that lords it over humans but actually doesn't know that much about anything other than themselves. Their only common enemy is the strix, but their number vary from what the GM decides and who knows what they really are/want. That gives them the most potential for discovery and, I think, maybe the widest range of possible stories (with Changelings being a close second I'd say). So if any supernatural template is perfect for Lovecraftian horror, I'd say it's vampires. They don't have any reference to ungodly poweful entities that they could compare elder gods and the such to and they're much more likely to feel lost and helpless against them. I mean, a Werewolf who takes the Luna/wolf mythos seriously could suggest that &quot;Ok, that Cthulhu thing sounds pretty powerful, but we've heard about Idigams and stuff like that. Even if it's more powerful than that, we're backed by one of the most powerful spirits ever, so what's there to fear ?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T14:39:35-07:00","id":964536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fire_vampire\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/static/images/icons/enwiki-25.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fire_vampire\" target=\"_blank\"> List of Great Old Ones - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fire_vampire\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fire_vampire </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yes. Do it.<br /> <br /> I will note that vampires the concept in of itself was originally seen as very lovecraftian. And some of those ideas have carried over. The century old creatures, long since dead. who have developed alien minds. With machinations that last far beyond mortal's lifespans. We're just so used to the idea now, because we've had so much exposure to it. It's lost some of its fright and edge. And our development of technology and understanding of history allows us to hold on to those idea better. We have sexy vampires. for good or ill. and if you want to go back futher We had Liches to scary the ssht out of us.<br /> <br /> I will say the writes have done a good job of trailing that arc from tragic victim to Monster.<br /> <br /> Also related<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://66.media.tumblr.com/tumblr_m2lnbjkEL31qzd219o1_500.gif\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://66.media.tumblr.com/tumblr_m2lnbjkEL31qzd219o1_500.gif\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://66.media.tumblr.com/tumblr_m2lnbjkEL31qzd219o1_500.gif\" target=\"_blank\"> https://66.media.tumblr.com/tumblr_m2lnbjkEL31qzd219o1_500.gif </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T01:14:48-07:00","id":964844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yarrumkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/963812-vampire-and-the-h-p-lovecraft-mythos?p=964048#post964048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So would you say that making a Vampire game based on the Cthulhu mythos would be a good idea? This game is going to be centered on the premise of dealing with the cults of certain Cthulhu mythos Elder Gods. And most of my players if not all are used to playing the fantasy aspect of roleplaying games like Pathfinder.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the most part just do what you would for a mortal groop. The main diffidence is that vampires have a reason to go poking about these things without some cult cover up, their higher up hears about it and says &quot;to look into this&quot; and they do or they realise something odd is going on and opt to find out what before it becomes a problem.<br /> The real question is which group of blood suckers you want exploring things. The Ordo and clans Meket and Nosferatu are the most likely to stumble across such things but anyone with the Herd merit amongst others might also hear about such things. Remember that where humans should want rid of the thing that shouldn't be a vampire may see it as something to be used, this thing overpowers an elder by a greater degree than the elder overpowers them so why not make use of it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T18:46:30-07:00","id":965978,"title":"","content":"Every World of Darkness (Classic or New) or Chronicle of Darkness game I have or ever will run features at very least Lovecraftian themes and motifs, if not a central focus (and many have had or will have it as their central focus). If you can find players who enjoy it and you do it well, you'll have some amazing times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 09-10-2016, 08:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T05:00:07-07:00","id":971257,"title":"","content":"I have a campaign concept, yet to be run, where Kindred are essentially the guardians of our world against supernatural threats from beyond. They already exist on the periphery, that shadowy edge of the known where beyond is nothing but darkness and that which dwells in it.<br /> <br /> I like it - it gives vampires both something to be afraid of and something to do other than whine about their immortality. For bonus points, the campaign starts off in Edwardian England. &quot;Black Goat of the Woods&quot; takes on a whole extra layer of horror when you really can get lost in the woods and the only torches you have are the burning kind. Think of it as a mix of Arthur Machen's Great God Pan with Wilkie Collin's Woman in White, and a little dose of the atmosphere of the computer game Alien: Isolation.<br /> <br /> Angst is such weak sauce when you've tasted fear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#D3D3D3\"><i>Fnord!</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11763-knasser","name":"knasser","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11763_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T07:40:57-07:00","id":971312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>knasser</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/963812-vampire-and-the-h-p-lovecraft-mythos?p=971257#post971257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a campaign concept, yet to be run, where Kindred are essentially the guardians of our world against supernatural threats from beyond. They already exist on the periphery, that shadowy edge of the known where beyond is nothing but darkness and that which dwells in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires are the only supernatural that need humanity and therefore the only one they can truly rely on to keep them safe and numerous is my opening argument should anyone claim humans would be better off wiping them out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T07:55:52-07:00","id":971318,"title":"","content":"The Great Old Ones and Outer Gods are no less horrifying just because you are now a vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T15:30:41-07:00","id":971542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gallus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/963812-vampire-and-the-h-p-lovecraft-mythos?p=971318#post971318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Great Old Ones and Outer Gods are no less horrifying just because you are now a vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's worth remembering that the Antediluvians from Masquerade were very similiar to the Great Old Ones in narrative structure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T16:48:57-07:00","id":971578,"title":"","content":"I'm curious, do you want to directly put your players up against monsters from the mythos, or do you want a lovecraft-flavored campaign? If the former, I'm sure plenty of lovecraft monsters have been written up by fans for the system. For the latter, the Idigam, the True Fae, the Abyss, and the Machine all make good potential antagonists. You might also want to look at Leviathan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T11:52:22-07:00","id":972047,"title":"","content":"As I recall in the 1E OD book, there is a discussion of Dragons who truck with mythos type creatures for knowledge and power. I'd look at that for some ideas. Generally speaking, I think vampire mix with Mythos baddies quite well. As a general rule Vampires shy away from anything supernatural that is not themselves because quite frankly vampires don't like to reminded that they're not the only game in town and there might be bigger badder games in tow. <br /> <br /> So for example lets say a cotiere is out looking for a poacher and they corner him and suddenly his shirt rips in half and he's got a foot long vertical mouth on his torso full of teeth and two tongues, thats waaaaaay beyond normal for vamps. Even with protean, vampires don't do that. So automatically their dealing with shit that should not be and assuming they survive, they have to be wondering 'what the fuck did that?'.<br /> <br /> Likewise if they run into a lovecraft ghoul, at first they might assume that they're dealing with an case of Nosferatu but overtime with it starts wielding more and more magic that deviates further and further from Cruac and Theban sorcery, they start to think &quot;Uhmmm...what exactly are we dealing with here guys?&quot; <br /> <br /> I would say if you want to bring in the mythos is to slowly turn up the heat on the water. In lovecraft anything supernatural will freak out PCs early on. With vampires they will be making all sorts of assumptions that will get them into trouble or lead them in the wrong direction in the beginning. Work with those assumptions so when the reveal happens, that &quot;Oh fuck&quot; moment is that much sweeter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1031-youvegotwildtalents","name":"youvegotwildtalents","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T12:03:00-07:00","id":972056,"title":"","content":"Mick Farren wrote a vampire series that, eventually, linked them to the Great Old Ones, specifically as the remnants of one of their servitor races. Interesting views on vampirism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T12:46:56-07:00","id":972076,"title":"","content":"The Void style of Cruac from the up coming secrets of the covenants is clearly inspired by Lovecraft mythos. When you cast a Cruac spell you also summon this Void Creature from between the stars, which is made up of darkness and various animal body parts, unless you force it into human or animal form.<br /> <br /> Basically they're lovecraftian familiars as a reward for serving Lovecraftian style Alien Gods. Compare that to the other two styles of Cruac, which seem almost natural in compareson to Void Magic, to the point where I see users of Void style creeping out even other members of the circle of the crone.<br /> <br /> What horrible price do this Vampires pay fir such alien servants?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T18:47:31-07:00","id":972262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>knasser</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/963812-vampire-and-the-h-p-lovecraft-mythos?p=971257#post971257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a campaign concept, yet to be run, where Kindred are essentially the guardians of our world against supernatural threats from beyond. They already exist on the periphery, that shadowy edge of the known where beyond is nothing but darkness and that which dwells in it.<br /> <br /> I like it - it gives vampires both something to be afraid of and something to do other than whine about their immortality. For bonus points, the campaign starts off in Edwardian England. &quot;Black Goat of the Woods&quot; takes on a whole extra layer of horror when you really can get lost in the woods and the only torches you have are the burning kind. Think of it as a mix of Arthur Machen's Great God Pan with Wilkie Collin's Woman in White, and a little dose of the atmosphere of the computer game Alien: Isolation.<br /> <br /> Angst is such weak sauce when you've tasted fear.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Khaibit Bloodline is pretty much just what your describing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T09:28:30-07:00","id":972572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/963812-vampire-and-the-h-p-lovecraft-mythos?p=963826#post963826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As for them having powers so what? It outranks their powers</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's like the vampire saying <i>&quot;Don't mess with me, I can bench press cars!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> and the elder one saying <i>&quot;Don't mess with me, I can bench press the sun!&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T10:50:15-07:00","id":972599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/963812-vampire-and-the-h-p-lovecraft-mythos?p=971312#post971312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vampires are the only supernatural that need humanity and therefore the only one they can truly rely on to keep them safe and numerous is my opening argument should anyone claim humans would be better off wiping them out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. If vampires are the worst the world of darkness contains, then that world is not dark enough. And if it does contain worse, then the vampires existing in the shadows between the light and the outer dark as they do, are naturally the first line of defence against that darkness. Whether they wish to be or not. I like to try and create the feeling for the players that they're standing at the edge of an abyss, that they've stepped from the world they knew to the lip of some great darkness that should terrify them. It's one of the things I really like about Blood and Smoke - the Vampires may be powerful and pull many strings, but there are things like the Stryx that are unknowable to them. Vampires and a lovecraftian feel go together surprisingly well. I tend not to go for the vast Cthulhu scale stuff - more the small strangeness. Goblins scratching at the windows and something hidden beneath the waters. But it's good to hint at greater terrors.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/963812-vampire-and-the-h-p-lovecraft-mythos?p=972262#post972262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Khaibit Bloodline is pretty much just what your describing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've not heard of them. But I really don't want the role to fall to some particular bloodline. That makes it sound like they're voluntary guardians, appointing themselves protectors. That's not what I want to go for. I want vampires in that role because they have to be. Nobody can escape being recruited because the threat has come to them. When some darkness befalls their city, say the dead are restless because of a stryx, or a manifestation of Pan is slowly consuming the city with madness, it falls to them to stop it because who else will save them if not themselves?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#D3D3D3\"><i>Fnord!</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11763-knasser","name":"knasser","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11763_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T11:59:35-07:00","id":972622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>knasser</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/963812-vampire-and-the-h-p-lovecraft-mythos?p=972599#post972599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That makes it sound like they're voluntary guardians, appointing themselves protectors. That's not what I want to go for. I want vampires in that role because they have to be. Nobody can escape being recruited because the threat has come to them. When some darkness befalls their city, say the dead are restless because of a stryx, or a manifestation of Pan is slowly consuming the city with madness, it falls to them to stop it because who else will save them if not themselves?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's quite interesting, the way you originally wrote it made it sound rather less subtle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T12:05:10-07:00","id":972625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/963812-vampire-and-the-h-p-lovecraft-mythos?p=972622#post972622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's quite interesting, the way you originally wrote it made it sound rather less subtle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you.<br /> <br /> Vampires are lonely shepherds. When a lion stalks the hills at dusk, the sheep will not protect them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#D3D3D3\"><i>Fnord!</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11763-knasser","name":"knasser","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11763_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T13:23:50-07:00","id":972678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>knasser</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/963812-vampire-and-the-h-p-lovecraft-mythos?p=972599#post972599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed. If vampires are the worst the world of darkness contains, then that world is not dark enough. And if it does contain worse, then the vampires existing in the shadows between the light and the outer dark as they do, are naturally the first line of defence against that darkness. Whether they wish to be or not. I like to try and create the feeling for the players that they're standing at the edge of an abyss, that they've stepped from the world they knew to the lip of some great darkness that should terrify them. It's one of the things I really like about Blood and Smoke - the Vampires may be powerful and pull many strings, but there are things like the Stryx that are unknowable to them. Vampires and a lovecraftian feel go together surprisingly well. I tend not to go for the vast Cthulhu scale stuff - more the small strangeness. Goblins scratching at the windows and something hidden beneath the waters. But it's good to hint at greater terrors.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I've not heard of them. But I really don't want the role to fall to some particular bloodline. That makes it sound like they're voluntary guardians, appointing themselves protectors. That's not what I want to go for. I want vampires in that role because they have to be. Nobody can escape being recruited because the threat has come to them. When some darkness befalls their city, say the dead are restless because of a stryx, or a manifestation of Pan is slowly consuming the city with madness, it falls to them to stop it because who else will save them if not themselves?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Mehh, I'm a bit hesitant to say vampires are part of the Lovecraft hierarchy, since they all pretty much agree that discovery of their existence would lead to their extinction. The horror of Lovecraft isn't that there are alien monsters out there, it's that there are <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>invincible</b></span> alien monsters out there. Humanity is completely helpless to defend itself against such creatures, and we should thank whatever gods exist that they deign to give us the bliss of ignorance.<br /> <br /> But when it comes to the Chronicles of Darkness, it seems like humanity is the one holding the cards. If they found out the supernatural existed, they'd go to war, a war that most splats seem to agree they would be victorious.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you want a more Lovecraft feel, I'd say that Mummies and Geists are more appropriate. Mummies because they're can't be permanently defeated and have cults of mortals dedicated to them. And Geists because they've seen what lays beyond death and decided a second chance at life was worth cohabiting a body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-19-2016, 04:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T13:30:53-07:00","id":972682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mehh, I'm a bit hesitant to say vampires are part of the Lovecraft hierarchy </div> </div> </div>They didn't say that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/963812-vampire-and-the-h-p-lovecraft-mythos?p=972678#post972678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But when it comes to the Chronicles of Darkness, it seems like humanity is the one holding the cards. If they found out the supernatural existed, they'd go to war, a war that most splats seem to agree they would be victorious.</div> </div> </div> </div>No they don't. Individual vampires can be killed. The vampire species isn't going anywhere. I can't think of any line apart from maybe Hunter where that's true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T13:57:04-07:00","id":972702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/963812-vampire-and-the-h-p-lovecraft-mythos?p=972682#post972682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> No they don't. Individual vampires can be killed. The vampire species isn't going anywhere. I can't think of any line apart from maybe Hunter where that's true.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought the whole point about the masquerade being in place was because vampires realized they couldn't survive publicly anymore? If that's not the case, then what's stopping them from coming out and taking over?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T15:17:28-07:00","id":972765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/963812-vampire-and-the-h-p-lovecraft-mythos?p=972702#post972702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the whole point about the masquerade being in place was because vampires realized they couldn't survive publicly anymore? If that's not the case, then what's stopping them from coming out and taking over?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not about the entire vampire race being wiped out. It's about the vampire Nyrufa being killed. They don't hide because they fear extinction. They promote the Masquerade because if one member of your coterie is 'outed,' then it's not long until people connect the dots and you wake up to someone shoving a stake in your heart before they lop off your head.<br /> <br /> The survival of the individual, notably yourself, is what the Masquerade is all about.<br /> <br /> There's covenants dedicated to eradicating the Masquerade, but even they realize it's going to take a gradual acceptance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T15:32:26-07:00","id":972775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/963812-vampire-and-the-h-p-lovecraft-mythos?p=972765#post972765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not about the entire vampire race being wiped out. It's about the vampire Nyrufa being killed. They don't hide because they fear extinction. They promote the Masquerade because if one member of your coterie is 'outed,' then it's not long until people connect the dots and you wake up to someone shoving a stake in your heart before they lop off your head.<br /> <br /> The survival of the individual, notably yourself, is what the Masquerade is all about.<br /> <br /> There's covenants dedicated to eradicating the Masquerade, but even they realize it's going to take a gradual acceptance.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Ah, got it. So like almost everything else in Kindred society, the masquerade is self serving. Kind of obvious now that I say it out loud.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T15:38:35-07:00","id":972778,"title":"","content":"Just jumping in but I find the idea of a circle worshiping a Dark Young and a group of Ordo trying to stop them from summoning more to be an awesome plot idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T16:21:42-07:00","id":972809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/963812-vampire-and-the-h-p-lovecraft-mythos?p=972778#post972778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just jumping in but I find the idea of a circle worshiping a Dark Young and a group of Ordo trying to stop them from summoning more to be an awesome plot idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. This sort of plot seed is excellent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T16:34:24-07:00","id":972816,"title":"","content":"Pretty much on the nose about the self serving masquerade. But is worth noting that a dedicated humanity can fuck a city of kindred's night. Cleaning out a neighborhood is definitely something a cell of hunters can tackle wiping a city would be harder would be a terribly hard fought battle, but it's quote unquote doable.<br /> <br /> But vamps are like herbies they can come back. Humanity forgets them. and then they awaken from the long sleep and propagate again, come from outside the quarantine zones, breaking curses and seals. Because the origins of vamps can't be defined an ST is well within their purview to set the stage as they wish.<br /> <br /> The CofD has the theme and mood that, you can make the world a better place. but it's hard and requires upkeep. Pulling from Hunter. How long do you keep the Vigil going?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T16:41:34-07:00","id":972821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/963812-vampire-and-the-h-p-lovecraft-mythos?p=972678#post972678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mehh, I'm a bit hesitant to say vampires are part of the Lovecraft hierarchy, since they all pretty much agree that discovery of their existence would lead to their extinction. The horror of Lovecraft isn't that there are alien monsters out there, it's that there are <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>invincible</b></span> alien monsters out there. Humanity is completely helpless to defend itself against such creatures, and we should thank whatever gods exist that they deign to give us the bliss of ignorance.<br /> <br /> But when it comes to the Chronicles of Darkness, it seems like humanity is the one holding the cards. If they found out the supernatural existed, they'd go to war, a war that most splats seem to agree they would be victorious.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you want a more Lovecraft feel, I'd say that Mummies and Geists are more appropriate. Mummies because they're can't be permanently defeated and have cults of mortals dedicated to them. And Geists because they've seen what lays beyond death and decided a second chance at life was worth cohabiting a body.</div> </div> </div> </div>Michael already pointed out that's not quite what I said (also, thumbs up gender neutral pronoun 'they' club <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ). But just to add to the other points you raise, I think mummies actually fit less well for a Lovecraftian game. I actually don't know the Mummy line and maybe you could play up the arbitrary / meaninglessness nature of existence and produce a somewhat bleak and uncaring universe feel, but I think that the immortality and the fact that mummies have a purpose goes against making players feel the true horror of a lovecraftian universe. Not necessarily of course - you can make most things work. For example, you could focus on the way all of human civilizations and achievements fall with time. A kind of Ozymandias / Gaze on my works view. Again, I haven't read Mummy so maybe that actually is the focus. But for what I want - fear of the unknown, fragility of existence - immortality and the benefit of a long and mystical view on existence would probably detract for it. It kind of depends whether you're playing up the uncaringness of the universe aspect or the fear / horror aspect of Lovecraft. For me, it's the latter that is most interesting.<br /> <br /> I also think in a Lovecraftian universe, hammering home the Masquerade is not quite as critical. Important, don't mistake me, but the reason it's needed in a vanilla V:tR game is because there needs to be something out there that keeps vampires in check, something to alarm them and restrain them. Elders are the other popular one for this role. But if you're playing a Lovecraftian vampire game, you already have a strong contender for that slot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/963812-vampire-and-the-h-p-lovecraft-mythos?p=972778#post972778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just jumping in but I find the idea of a circle worshiping a Dark Young and a group of Ordo trying to stop them from summoning more to be an awesome plot idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh. That's a nice idea. Chess-playing elder vampires and princes with Majesty up the wazoo become clich\u00e9 with time. But encountering an unhinged group of vampires devoted to worshipping some blood-dripping tree monster, now THAT is creepy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> *Yoink*<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#D3D3D3\"><i>Fnord!</i></span>","edited":{"userid":11763,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11763-knasser","user":"knasser","date":". 09-19-2016, 07:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11763-knasser","name":"knasser","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11763_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T16:53:12-07:00","id":972825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MercSet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/963812-vampire-and-the-h-p-lovecraft-mythos?p=972816#post972816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But vamps are like herbies they can come back. Humanity forgets them. and then they awaken from the long sleep</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <img src=\"http://i67.tinypic.com/6i5usk.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">?</span></span></b><br /> <br /> Actually, I see what you mean. Chained up, forgotten... but waiting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#D3D3D3\"><i>Fnord!</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11763-knasser","name":"knasser","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11763_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T17:36:26-07:00","id":972839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>knasser</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/963812-vampire-and-the-h-p-lovecraft-mythos?p=972821#post972821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Michael already pointed out that's not quite what I said (also, thumbs up gender neutral pronoun 'they' club <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ). But just to add to the other points you raise, I think mummies actually fit less well for a Lovecraftian game. I actually don't know the Mummy line and maybe you could play up the arbitrary / meaninglessness nature of existence and produce a somewhat bleak and uncaring universe feel, but I think that the immortality and the fact that mummies have a purpose goes against making players feel the true horror of a lovecraftian universe. Not necessarily of course - you can make most things work. For example, you could focus on the way all of human civilizations and achievements fall with time. A kind of Ozymandias / Gaze on my works view. Again, I haven't read Mummy so maybe that actually is the focus. But for what I want - fear of the unknown, fragility of existence - immortality and the benefit of a long and mystical view on existence would probably detract for it. It kind of depends whether you're playing up the uncaringness of the universe aspect or the fear / horror aspect of Lovecraft. For me, it's the latter that is most interesting.<br /> <br /> I also think in a Lovecraftian universe, hammering home the Masquerade is not quite as critical. Important, don't mistake me, but the reason it's needed in a vanilla V:tR game is because there needs to be something out there that keeps vampires in check, something to alarm them and restrain them. Elders are the other popular one for this role. But if you're playing a Lovecraftian vampire game, you already have a strong contender for that slot.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I haven't read Mummy, either. But the one thing I understand about it is that your character can not (permanently) be destroyed. Whatever magic they used to become what they are bestowed them with true immortality. No matter how many times you destroy them, they will rise again, their body reconstructing itself throughout the ages. And many of them have mortal cults dedicated to servicing their needs. An unstoppable creature with mortal servants is pretty close to Lovecraft's vision.<br /> <br /> I've also been told they have semi-god level powers, such as creating sandstorms on the spot!<br /> <br /> They would make good cross over antagonists. Especially if they can make witty quips about &quot;final&quot; death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-19-2016, 08:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T18:27:34-07:00","id":972861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>knasser</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/963812-vampire-and-the-h-p-lovecraft-mythos?p=972825#post972825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i67.tinypic.com/6i5usk.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">?</span></span></b><br /> <br /> Actually, I see what you mean. Chained up, forgotten... but waiting.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Herpes_simplex\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/da/He